data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span` of native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` reported **8 bytes**. The spans allocated, wrote, and iterated without issue. This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5 when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class types — they're valid anywhere a regular unmanaged type is, including `stackalloc`.
